0009:     Complete the scene by adding the point-reflected copy of the colored object across the central marker.
0010: 
0011:     Input structure
0012:     - The grid has odd dimensions, a dominant background, and a center-row marker color appearing only at the left edge, center, and right edge.
0013:     - A single divider color fills the center column except for the center marker.
0014:     - All remaining foreground pixels form the object to copy, entirely on the left side of the divider.
0015:     Rule
0016:     - Keep the input unchanged.
0017:     - For every object pixel, paint the pixel rotated 180 degrees around the center marker with the same color.
0018:     Key insight
0019:     - The center marker is the rotation center; the yellow-looking divider is not mirrored, it only separates the source from the empty target side.
0020:     """
